From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:23:30 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 08/43] shader,gpu: resolve heap-loaded view addresses and
 widen native complement masks

Ray-tracing shadow-mask trace programs read 64-bit title buffer addresses
from descriptors loaded out of the bindless resource heap (or dynamically
indexed tables) rather than static descriptor tables. Previously
Lower::view_address only handled static tables, failing those shaders with
'a descriptor read only as data'.

Add a per-view-heap buffer-address table (SLOT_VIEW_ADDRESSES = 252,
SLOT_STRIDES_COUNT pairs of (lo, hi) dwords) maintained in HostHeap::mirror
and bound as a root SRV in victory-gpu, and read it from Lower::view_address
for ResourceHeap and dynamically indexed Table loads.

Also allow native wave32/wave64 compute shaders (MaskData::Console,
!local) to check all_lane_blocks and trigger widen() on MASK_ELSEWHERE
when a complement mask sits inside a per-lane skip, unlocking the final
ray-tracing shadow-mask trace program and bringing all 64 BVH trace
programs to 64/64 emitted and DXIL-validated.

(cherry picked from commit ea40c9a9ca721011c850ca36b2d8f2dc65ef25ce)
